  "narrative": {
    "overview": "OpenSense extends the user-approved Glacier Blue Material 3 world established on 16 October 2026. A real XUV500 cutout rests on a low oval platform on Vehicle; quiet headings, aligned readings, tonal actions and grouped status rows make it an automotive companion. The image is illustrative, not proof of a selected variant's equipment. Retain the existing asset; 3D remains deferred.\n\nThe built ownership extension uses the same world for private phone records: full task routes, readable forms, grouped lists and useful empty states. Material 3 supplies native structure and interaction. Dark is the fresh-install default; an explicit light choice persists. This remains a portrait-only phone product with Vehicle, Climate, Media and Insights as its four main destinations. Vehicle generation, simulation and appearance remain in Settings without an onboarding gate. Private phone storage and deliberate Android handoffs constrain the interface; cloud accounts and Wear OS are outside the confirmed scope.",
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the real XUV500 cutout/platform and the four Material destinations.",
      "Do use Material roles, system type scaling, readable units and vector icons.",
      "Do let date/time actions and reminder chips wrap with complete labels.",
      "Do label phone estimates, manual records, simulation and head-unit data distinctly.",
      "Do preserve scrolling, native Back and visible recovery actions."
    ],
    "northStar": "A calm garage display",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Glacier Blue actions on midnight tonal surfaces, with a separate cloud-light scheme.",
      "System Material typography, vector icons and native controls.",
      "A photographic vehicle signature with restrained diagrammatic data elsewhere.",
      "Scrollable ownership routes with honest source, permission and empty-state language."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't replace the established world or add vehicle imagery to every ownership form.",
      "Don't expose internal route keys or UUIDs as app-bar titles.",
      "Don't leave adjustable controls without focused purpose and value/unit descriptions.",
      "Don't imply Android handoffs prove completion.",
      "Don't claim synthetic/emulator evidence verifies physical-device or vehicle behavior."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "section": "colors",
        "body": "Keep simulated, phone-derived, manually entered and head-unit values visibly distinguishable; color alone is insufficient.",
        "name": "The Source Clarity Rule"
      },
      {
        "section": "typography",
        "body": "App bars show “Trip details”, “Edit fill-up” and “Edit reminder” for record routes; never expose internal route keys or record IDs as titles.",
        "name": "The Human Context Rule"
      }
    ]
  },
